<title>SWITZERLAND: Memphis top world cargo airport in Dec 96 - report.</title>
<headline>Memphis top world cargo airport in Dec 96 - report.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier Federal Express was the world's busiest cargo airport in December 1996, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI) in a survey of 487 airports worldwide.</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in December 1996, with the volume they handled and the percentage change over December 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  Memphis		 181,527   up   19.8pct</p>
<p> 2  Los Angeles	   151,727   down  6.6</p>
<p> 3  Miami		   149,237   down  0.9</p>
<p> 4  Hong Kong	     148,185   up   13.15</p>
<p> 5  Tokyo-Narita	  147,301   up    3.7</p>
<p> 6  New York		136,152   up    5.3</p>
<p> 7  Frankfurt	     132,340   up    2.3</p>
<p> 8  Seoul		   129,185   up   18.3</p>
<p> 9  Singapore	     113,183   up   13.6</p>
<p> 10 Louisville	    112,444   down  4.2</p>
<p> 11 Chicago		 111,394   up    2.8</p>
<p> 12 Amsterdam	     104,630   up    6.8</p>
<p> 13 Anchorage	     101,883   up   20.5</p>
<p> 14 London Heathrow	95,845   down  0.2</p>
<p> 15 Paris-CDG		86,796   up   14.4</p>
<p> 16 New York Newark	80,795   up    1.7</p>
<p> 17 Tokyo Haneda	   77,504   up    1.2</p>
<p> 18 Taipei		   75,916   up   13.1</p>
<p> 19 Atlanta		  71,957   down  1.3</p>
<p> 20 Dallas Fort Worth    68,465   up    2.0</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
